  "_comment": "CANONICAL SYNTHETIC-ENTITY REGISTRY. Single source of truth (AI-CODING-CONVENTIONS §1.1, §4 'single source') for every de-attributed organisation in the RHTP demo corpus. Wave 1 de-attributed three screens by hand and the same names survived in 30+ other files; this registry exists so that never happens again: names, short/graph forms, phones, emails, domains and street addresses are owned HERE and nowhere else. RULE THIS ENCODES: a real place name may appear as a LOCATION (county, city, ZIP, lat/lng, map label) but never inside an ORGANISATION name; tribal and people names may not appear in an organisation name at all. Consequently county/city/ZIP/lat/lng values are NOT substituted anywhere in this file — 'Bennett', 'Oglala Lakota', 'Pine Ridge', 'Winner', 'Rapid City' remain as geography, and county keys in particular are load-bearing for the networkAdequacy engine. Phones use the NANP-reserved 555-0100..555-0199 fictitious range; emails and domains use RFC 2606 example.org. The oldNames / oldPhones / oldDomains / oldStreets fields are PROVENANCE: they record what was replaced so the coherence sweep can prove zero residue, and they are the only place an old name may legitimately appear.",
